        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google-meet): neutralize attendance CSV formulas [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users exporting Google Meet attendance data to CSV could open a file where a participant-provided display name is treated as a spreadsheet formula instead of plain text.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nGoogle Meet attendance CSV rendering now prefixes formula-like cell values with a spreadsheet text marker before normal CSV escaping. The change stays inside the Google Meet plugin export/CLI formatter and does not change attendance collection, OAuth, calendar lookup, transcript export, or JSON output.\n\n## User Impact\n\nGoogle Meet attendance CSV output remains readable, while participant names that begin with spreadsheet formula triggers are preserved as text when the CSV is opened in common spreadsheet tools.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused test: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/google-meet/src/cli.test.ts`\n- Result: `extensions/google-meet/src/cli.test.ts` passed with 49 tests.\n- Coverage added for both `googlemeet attendance --format csv` stdout and exported `attendance.csv` bundle output.\n\n## AI Assistance\n\nThis PR was prepared with AI assistance.\n",
